 "researcher_notes": "Not an existing row. The roster has the Gas Transmission Northwest main line (P0231) and the GTN Xpress Expansion (P3171), but nothing for this lateral. A Federal Register notice from August 2012 describes the application under docket CP12-494 for about 24.3 miles of 20-inch pipe from the Ione Compressor Station to the proposed Carty Generating Station in Morrow County, Oregon. The FERC approved projects table for 2012 to 2014 lists 24.30 miles and 175 MMcf/d with no compression. The EIA August 2026 release (sheet Historical Projects, Excel row 807) lists the Carty Lateral Project as Completed in November 2015, 24.4 miles, 20 inch, 175 MMcf/d, cost 54.3 million dollars. EIA length of 24.4 differs slightly from the 24.3 in the two FERC sources, which agree, so 24.3 is staged. Length is about 39 km, above the 25 km threshold. Status operating rests on EIA alone. Parent company was not sourced, so it is left blank. Capacity is the lateral's own delivery capacity. Route not researched; the route would come from the FERC environmental filings. No route fields staged."
}